# Backend learnings (packages/backend)

Contextual advice for future tasks in the Convex backend. Reference before working on
partner-API, webhook, trigger, or convex-test tasks.

## Partner API / webhooks (added 2026-07-17)

- **Single choke-point for table-change side effects**: `convex/functions.ts` wraps every
  mutation with a convex-helpers `Triggers` registry. To react to ALL writes on a table
  (regardless of which mutation performs them), register a trigger there — do not wire
  per-mutation calls. Partner webhook emission lives in `convex/lib/webhookEmission.ts`
  and is registered for `rsvps` and `events`.
- **Trigger ordering matters**: triggers fire immediately at each `ctx.db` write. If a
  trigger reads sibling rows (e.g. webhook identity resolution reads `guestContacts`),
  those rows must be written BEFORE the row that fires the trigger. This is why
  `submitGuestRequest` upserts `guestContacts` before inserting the RSVP.
- **Guest identity**: synthetic clerk ids (`guest:<phoneHash>`) helpers live in
  `convex/lib/guestIdentity.ts` (extracted from rsvps.ts). Guest plaintext phone is
  durably stored only in `guestContacts` (by design; handoff rows expire).
- **API keys**: stored SHA-256-hashed (`lib/apiKeys.ts` reuses `hashOpaqueValue`).
  Webhook endpoint secrets are stored readable (AES needs key recovery) — an accepted,
  documented tradeoff (docs/partner-api.md).
- **HTTP surface**: `/api/v1/*` httpActions live in `convex/apiV1.ts` (auth middleware
  in `lib/apiRequestAuth.ts`), backed by internal functions in `convex/apiV1Data.ts`.
  Deliberately no CORS. `API_VERSION` and webhook event types come from
  `@coucou/sdk/api-v1` — single source shared with consumers; keep the sdk consumer
  helpers byte-compatible with `convex/lib/webhookCrypto.ts` (roundtrip-tested in
  `packages/sdk/__tests__/webhook-consumer.test.ts`).

## convex-test gotchas (bun test)

- **Scheduled function leaks**: mutations that `ctx.scheduler.runAfter(0, ...)` leave real
  timers that can fire after a test file ends → "Write outside of transaction" /
  "test began while previous transaction was still open" in LATER files. Either
  (a) `vi.useFakeTimers()` in beforeEach + `testBackend.finishAllScheduledFunctions(vi.runAllTimers)`
  after each mutation (see webhook-pipeline.test.ts, text-blasts.test.ts), or
  (b) track backends and drain in afterEach (see rsvp-guest-handoff.test.ts).
  Never switch to fake timers AFTER a real 0-delay timer is already queued — that races.
- **Parallel component calls fail**: `Promise.all` over aggregate `count()` calls inside
  one query throws "Bad queryId" under convex-test. Run component sub-queries
  sequentially.
- **httpAction tests**: `testBackend.fetch("/api/v1/...", init)` works; module map must
  include `http.ts` and every module reachable from the routed handlers.
- **Aggregate component**: register with `testBackend.registerComponent("rsvpAggregate",
  schema, modules)` importing from `node_modules/@convex-dev/aggregate/dist/esm/component/*`
  (copy the block from an existing test).
- **WebCrypto in mutations**: `crypto.subtle.digest` and `crypto.getRandomValues` work in
  the Convex default runtime and in convex-test — hashing/keygen inside mutations is fine.

## TypeScript

- Under TS 5.7+ libs, annotate WebCrypto-bound byte helpers to return
  ArrayBuffer-backed arrays (`new Uint8Array(new ArrayBuffer(n))`, inferred return type)
  or `crypto.subtle` calls fail on `Uint8Array<ArrayBufferLike>` vs `BufferSource`.
